.\" who.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX who(1) utility, which this
.\" tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/WHO.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/WHO.
.TH WHO 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
who \- display who is on the system
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Who
is not provided on maux.
maux is a single-user system with no user or group accounts:
ProDOS's own access byte carries no owner or group at all
(docs/ANACHRONISMS.md sec W2).
